#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0276 expect=violation domain=TS
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a record exists with TSPARMCD equal to 'STYPE' and TSVAL equal to 'INTERVENTIONAL', but TSVAL is empty for the record where TSPARMCD equals 'TRT'.
#note "Two TRT records, both with an empty TSVAL -> BOTH rows are reported. This is the fixture the pre-split Dataset sensitivity could not produce: it collapsed them to one finding."
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=2 TSSEQ=2
#expectViolationAt row=3 TSSEQ=3
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S01 | TS | 1 | STYPE | INTERVENTIONAL
S01 | TS | 2 | TRT | 
S01 | TS | 3 | TRT | 
S01 | TS | 4 | TITLE | A Study of Drug X
---
